  "semantics": "Line 1: n, 1<=n<=10^5; line 2: n integers 0<=a_i<=2*10^9, non-decreasing (exponent markup restored from the original statement). Output the minimum count of added powers 2^b (b>=0) making the total 2^v-1 for some v>=0. With S=sum 2^a_i, the optimum is v=bitlength(S) and the answer bitlength(S)-popcount(S), a unique integer (up to 2000000011). Oracle carries equal exponents upward in one sorted pass; independently checked by exhaustive minimum-coin DP over every v for small inputs and by big-integer bit-plane popcount for large ones.",
  "oracle": "Single sorted pass over runs of equal exponents with an integer carry: before each new value, flush carry bits into positions pos..value-1 (counting set bits and the highest set position); then add the run length. Answer = highest set bit + 1 - number of set bits of S = sum 2^a_i. Minimality: any target 2^v-1 >= S needs v >= bitlength(S); the gap 2^v-1-S needs popcount(gap) powers (binary representation is the unique minimum), and popcount(2^v-1-S) = v - popcount(S) is minimised at v = bitlength(S). b>=0 and v>=0 never bind since S>=1.",
  "bruteChecks": 2891,
  "bruteReference": {
    "exhaustiveMinCoinDP": "Every non-decreasing array for (n,max a) in (1,13),(2,11),(3,9),(4,7),(5,6),(6,5),(7,4),(8,3): 2061 inputs. Reference enumerates every v with 2^v-1>=S and takes a literal min-coin DP over powers of two for the gap (no popcount formula); oracle and the big-integer reference both asserted equal.",
    "randomMinCoinDP": "400 fixed-seed (305777) random arrays n<=12, a<=10 vs min-coin DP.",
    "randomBigInt": "300 fixed-seed random arrays n<=300 with clustered or wide exponents up to 2*10^9 vs exact big-integer reference (runs split at gaps>40, which carries from <=10^5 items cannot cross; S built from count bit-planes; popcount/bitlength read from the integer).",
    "extras": "All 130 authored extras (including every n=10^5 case) re-derived by the big-integer reference.",
